# 🚩 Challenge: [Sleuthkit Intro]
![sleuthkit_intro_qn](sleuthkit_intro.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
Download the disk image and use mmls on it to find the size of the Linux partition. Connect to the remote checker service to check your answer and get the flag.

Note: if you are using the webshell, download and extract the disk image into /tmp not your home directory.

Download disk image
 Access checker program: nc chatelaine.cylabacademy.net 14158



### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/d8718cbbc14dcd9f9aad532a51d7a01b00e1715ca3b1d654dfef687d0b15cbf5/disk.img.gz
2. gunzip disk.img.gz
3. file disk.img
4. apt install sleuthkit
5. mmls disk.img(note the size of the disk image.)
6. nc chatelaine.cylabacademy.net 14158
7. Enter `size of the disk image` to get the flag.
```

---

## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Download the `disk.img.gz` file from challenge and extract it using `gunzip`.
2. Check the file using `file`.
3. Download `sleuthkit` if not installed before.
4. Check the `mmls disk.img` and the size of the disk will be displayed.
5. Connect the  `nc chatelaine.cylabacademy.net 14158` and enter the size of the disk image from `step4` and the flag will display.


